### 1. Health Check
GET http://localhost:3000/api/health

### 2. Root API Welcome
GET http://localhost:3000/

### 3. Get All Users
GET http://localhost:3000/api/users

### 4. User Signup (Successful)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ayush Jadhav",
  "email": "ayush@example.com",
  "password": "MySecretPassword123"
}

### 5. User Signup (Missing Fields - should fail with 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "incomplete@example.com"
}

### 6. User Signup (Short Password - should fail with 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bob",
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "123"
}

### 7. User Login (Successful)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ayush@example.com",
  "password": "MySecretPassword123"
}

### 8. User Login (Invalid Password - should fail with 401)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ayush@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword123"
}

### 9. User Login (Non-existent Email - should fail with 401)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "unknown@example.com",
  "password": "AnyPassword123"
}

### 10. User Login (Missing Fields - should fail with 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ayush@example.com"
}

### 11. Get Current User Profile (Protected - Success with Bearer Token)
# Replace <YOUR_JWT_TOKEN> with the token obtained from login
GET http://localhost:3000/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_JWT_TOKEN>

### 12. Get Current User Profile (Protected - Missing Token should fail with 401)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/auth/me

### 13. Get Current User Profile (Protected - Invalid Token should fail with 401)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid_jwt_token_12345


